text:
Q: How can I customize keyboard behaviour in HTML select menus? A: <h3>Design ad hoc string comparer depending on locale</h3>
<p>Define a helper function which depends on locale to compare the strings. For Swedish, <code>A</code> and <code>Ä</code> should be different.
For other languages such as English, use browser's collator and thus they will be treated as equal.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function localeAwareEquals(a, b, locale) {
  if (locale.startsWith('sv')) { // such as 'sv-SE'
    return a === b;
  }
  return new Intl.Collator(locale, { sensitivity: 'base' }).compare(a, b) === 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Test result:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>console.log(localeAwareEquals('A', `Ä`, 'en-US')); // true
console.log(localeAwareEquals('A', `Ä`, 'sv-SE')); // false
</code></pre>
<h3>Test it with web page, using en-US locale</h3>
<p>A test web page, using English locale first:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;html&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
&lt;select id=&quot;menu&quot;&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;Please select&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;Ä&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;Å&lt;/option&gt;
  &lt;option&gt;A&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;
&lt;script&gt;
function localeAwareEquals(a, b, locale) {
  if (locale.startsWith('sv')) { // such as 'sv-SE'
    return a === b;
  }
  return new Intl.Collator(locale, { sensitivity: 'base' }).compare(a, b) === 0;
}

const menu = document.getElementById('menu');
document.addEventListener('keydown', e =&gt; {
  //console.log('key pressed: ' + e.key);
  if (e.key.length === 1) {
    const typed = e.key;
    for (let i = 0; i &lt; menu.options.length; i++) {
      const optionText = menu.options[i].textContent;
      if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, 'en-US')) {
        menu.selectedIndex = i;
        break;
      }
    }
  }
});
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Test result: When the key <code>A</code> is pressed, the item <code>Ä</code> is selected.</p>
<h3>Next test: change to Swedish locale sv-SE</h3>
<p>Change this section of code:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>      if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, 'en-US')) {
        menu.selectedIndex = i;
        break;
      }
</code></pre>
<p>... to:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>      if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, 'sv-SE')) {
        menu.selectedIndex = i;
        break;
      }
</code></pre>
<p>Reload the page and hit <code>A</code>. Now item <code>A</code> is selected, both <code>Ä</code> and <code>Å</code> are skipped.</p>
<h3>Use the real locale</h3>
<p>We can now change that code section to use real browser locale, but first we need to know how to get such info. To show current language/locale:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>console.log(navigator.language); // en-US
</code></pre>
<p>So the section of code should be changed as:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>      if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, navigator.language)) {
        menu.selectedIndex = i;
        break;
      }
</code></pre>
<p>Reload the page and hit <code>A</code> again, and now item <code>Ä</code> is selected because my browser locale is <code>en-US</code>. On a Swedish environment it will show <code>A</code> instead.</p>
<h3>Limitation</h3>
<p>This only works if the key is pressed while that menu is <strong>not</strong> already focused or selected. If however the user manually clicks on the menu and its
pull-down menu is shown, then it will fall back to browser's default behavior to always ignore the diacritics.</p>
<p>Changing this code:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>document.addEventListener('keydown', e =&gt; {
   ...
   if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, 'sv-SE')) { ... }
});
</code></pre>
<p>... to:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>menu.addEventListener('keydown', e =&gt; {
   ...
   if (localeAwareEquals(optionText[0], typed, 'sv-SE')) { ... }
});
</code></pre>
<p>Would have no effect at all. It appears at the pull-down menu level it does not accept <code>'keydown'</code> event, only <code>window</code> or <code>document</code> elements do. Registering such event to menu item also generates no error, though.</p>
<h3>References</h3>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Collator" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Intl.Collator - JavaScript | MDN</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/language" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Navigator: language property - Web APIs | MDN</a></li>
</ul>
